Now I see the flow. In `tt_face_load_colr_layers`, there's a check:
```c
if ( palette_entry_index != 0xFFFF                                 &&
     palette_entry_index >= face->palette_data.num_palette_entries )
{
  error = FT_THROW( Invalid_Table );
  goto Error;
}
```

This checks `palette_entry_index` against `num_palette_entries`. But wait - `face->palette_data.num_palette_entries` is set during `tt_face_load_cpal`. Let me look at ttcpal.c again to see how `num_palette_entries` is set:

<｜｜DSML｜｜>
<parameter=thought>Let me look at ttcpal.c to see how num_palette_entries is set and whether there's a vulnerability there. The check in tt_face_load_colr_layers validates palette_entry_index against num_palette_entries, but if num_palette_entries is wrong (too large), the check would pass and then later the color index would be used to index into face->palette array which might be smaller.</｜｜DSML｜｜>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

